## Problem

The inference router treats configured or attested providers as executable even when the selected model is absent, credentials are unavailable, or the route cannot satisfy the turn. A model-not-found dispatch is then translated into a false “every provider is busy” response attributed to the named coworker and a local model, hiding the actual platform failure.

## Scope

In:
- derive canonical route readiness from the existing provider, connection, discovered-model, model-profile, capacity, credential, policy, and residency substrate;
- reconcile local discovery and active profiles atomically, and retire stale profiles before selection;
- on a model-not-found dispatch, reconcile and reroute once without looping;
- keep ordinary standing-coworker conversation out of onboarding classification unless the route is actually under setup;
- replace generic dead ends with typed, evidence-based failure categories and a platform/system recovery card;
- ensure synthetic failure content is not attributed to the coworker or an unverified model/provider;
- refactor duplicated readiness and failure-copy branches into one typed resolver and presenter (target about 20% of implementation effort).

Out:
- local model install/delete management already owned by BI-1FFDF4B1;
- the discovery_sweep constitutional gate owned by BI-2EFF90F2;
- broader local-only compliance policy owned by BI-BB337746;
- new persistence tables or parallel readiness state.

## Acceptance criteria

- A configured provider is displayed and routed as ready only when the requested turn has an executable, policy-eligible route at evaluation time.
- A stale local model profile cannot be selected after discovery reconciliation.
- A model-not-found response triggers one reconciliation/reroute attempt and records the actual terminal category.
- Busy, disconnected/credential, model-missing, policy-blocked, capability/context, and service-unavailable failures produce distinct honest guidance.
- Platform-generated recovery messages render as system failures and never claim the named coworker or a local model authored them.
- Standing COO conversation outside setup is not classified as onboarding solely because of the coworker.
- Regression tests reproduce the stale-profile/busy misdiagnosis and no-eligible-route attribution before the fix and pass afterward.
- The affected coworker thread is verified in the running portal with theme-aware shared UI primitives.

## Dependencies and related work

Related: BI-1FFDF4B1, BI-BB337746, BI-2EFF90F2, BI-2C50F548. This item coordinates with them but does not subsume their independent scope.

Context: customer dogfood evidence from coworker decision thread DI-2B3156C625AD on 2026-08-23.
